WEBVTT

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:08.190
If you're going to duel in your dad's 
place, I'll duel for Strong Ishijima.

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:09.580
Stop it!

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:14.530
The man Gongenzaka won't 
allow you to bully the weak!

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.710
My opponent in the first match is my 
former senior classmate Gen Ankokuji.

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:37.950
He insulted Yuya, opposed Gongenzaka 
Dojo's teachings and left.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:44.300
I must not lose this match!

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:48.190
That's the spirit!

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:49.560
Father!

00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:53.840
Noboru, battle wearing this new sash

00:00:53.840 --> 00:01:00.280
to further strengthen your immovable 
heart that you trained in my dojo!

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:04.760
Understood!

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:12.180
Implementing mass into Solid 
Vision has created Action Duels.

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:17.050
In duels where the field, monsters 
and duelists become one,

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:20.060
the people are caught in 
a frenzy of excitement!

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:24.360
Believe x Believe  Biri-Biri-Biri Buddies!

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:43.140
You!  The strongest card 
isn't about winning or losing

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:46.550
You!  At full speed  On the game

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:55.290
Swinging ma ma ma mind

00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:59.860
The soul's pendulum  Ultimate confusion

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.060
Impulse  Got it got it

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:07.270
Tough battles  Real revolution

00:02:13.630 --> 00:02:18.030
Everybody goin'  Break through the walls!

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:24.950
Infinite future  Get rid of indecision!

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:28.890
Make it Make it  Be courageous (Break it now)

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:32.290
Step ahead!  Take a step (Do it now)

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:42.570
The fun is only getting started!  
So everyone's a Believer!!

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:45.910
Believe x Believe  Biri-Biri-Biri Buddies!

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:55.950
Immovable Heart Tested

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:59.700
Maiami Championship!

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:03.530
This duelist festival is the 
gateway to becoming a pro duelist.

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:07.170
Those with passion have gathered here!

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:11.660
Yuzu won yesterday, and I'm up today.

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:14.800
Gongenzaka, Sora and I are going to win.

00:03:14.990 --> 00:03:17.100
We'll all make the second round!

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:22.280
Ouch!

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:26.750
That's Noboru Gongenzaka's battle sash!

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:30.460
That's his...

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:33.890
Wait!

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:35.580
Hurry!

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:38.860
Gongenzaka's match is starting soon!

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:41.120
Huh?  Where's Yuya?

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:43.200
He said that he'd be waiting for us.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:44.340
Over there!

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:47.040
It seems he's quickly getting further away.

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:52.360
Why did he take Gongenzaka's sash?

00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:54.980
He's probably Ankokuji's friend!

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:58.830
He'll do anything to win!

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:00.450
Ankokuji!

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:03.860
You're Noboru's friend Sakaki, right?

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:06.160
Don't you also have a match?

00:04:06.530 --> 00:04:09.830
Forget that!  This is 
important for Gongenzaka!

00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:12.330
I'll get his sash back!

00:04:20.210 --> 00:04:22.540
Everyone, thank you for coming

00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:27.500
to the second day of the 
tournament with excitement!

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:33.560
Allow me to introduce the two duelists 
who will battle in the first match!

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:36.320
Though unaffiliated, he's won 
six official matches in a row

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:39.700
to qualify for the Junior Youth Championship!

00:04:39.730 --> 00:04:42.360
Gen Ankokuji!

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:47.800
Facing him is Gongenzaka Dojo's 
successor with his Immovable Duel!

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:50.770
Noboru Gongenzaka!

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:54.540
That's a nice sash.  Did 
you get it from your dad?

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:59.210
Before an important match, the master 
gives a new sash to his student.

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:02.800
That is Gongenzaka Dojo's tradition.

00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:08.570
I'm using that tradition to my advantage.

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:09.390
What?

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:13.060
First, let's select the Field Spell!

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:17.680
Today's field will be... this!

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:23.440
Here we go!  Action Field on!

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:30.610
The Field Spell Calamity Cove activates!

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:36.600
A dense forest?  What a coincidence.

00:05:37.330 --> 00:05:40.550
Your friend is also currently in a forest.

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:42.650
What?

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:53.880
An ambush!

00:05:57.280 --> 00:05:58.470
What is it?

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:02.610
You fool!  You fell for our trap!

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:04.810
You'll have to deal with us.

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:09.740
How dare you!

00:06:10.350 --> 00:06:12.650
How dirty!

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:16.360
Hey, what happened to your unwavering heart?

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:18.740
You're very agitated.

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:23.720
I knew an immovable heart 
was nothing special.

00:06:23.720 --> 00:06:26.220
I'll do whatever it takes to win.

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:28.230
That's what a strong person does!

00:06:28.540 --> 00:06:32.340
That's why I left Gongenzaka Dojo.

00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:33.940
How dare you!

00:06:34.180 --> 00:06:37.020
I wonder if Yuya Sakaki is okay?

00:06:38.860 --> 00:06:42.510
If you want to save him, you 
have to defeat me quickly.

00:06:42.510 --> 00:06:45.630
Or will you immediately 
surrender because your friend

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:47.720
is more important than this match?

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:53.400
The match has already started.  Where's Yuya?

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:54.320
Yuzu?

00:06:54.320 --> 00:06:55.060
Yuya!

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:58.350
Tell Gongenzaka not to worry.

00:06:59.020 --> 00:07:01.640
That I promise to get his sash back.

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:03.400
Sash?

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:10.940
For my dojo's honor, I cannot 
surrender without battling!

00:07:11.920 --> 00:07:14.950
Then fight back in vain!

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:20.920
The duelists meet at the battlefield!

00:07:21.980 --> 00:07:23.370
Along with their monsters,

00:07:23.370 --> 00:07:27.390
they'll kick the ground and fly through 
the sky to move around the field!

00:07:28.390 --> 00:07:30.430
Witness...

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:33.130
...dueling's greatest evolution!

00:07:33.550 --> 00:07:35.600
Action!

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:36.870
Duel!

00:07:40.170 --> 00:07:42.070
I'll go first.

00:07:42.340 --> 00:07:46.750
I summon Granite Battleguard from my hand.

00:07:49.010 --> 00:07:51.180
When it's successfully summoned,

00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:54.960
I can Special Summon Boulder 
Battleguard from my hand.

00:07:56.440 --> 00:07:59.690
Whoa!  This is very nostalgic for me!

00:07:59.690 --> 00:08:02.780
These monsters are affiliated 
with Strong Ishijima!

00:08:02.780 --> 00:08:06.170
I set one card and end my turn.

00:08:07.350 --> 00:08:10.070
Now it's your turn.

00:08:10.470 --> 00:08:14.080
If you don't hurry, your friend 
is going to get pummeled.

00:08:16.970 --> 00:08:19.880
I'll finish you with a single strike!

00:08:19.880 --> 00:08:21.050
My turn!

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:28.410
When you have two or more 
monsters on your field,

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:31.860
I can Special Summon this card from my hand!

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:36.670
Appear, Superheavy Samurai Big Waraji!

00:08:37.800 --> 00:08:43.020
One Big Waraji counts as two 
monsters when I Tribute Summon!

00:08:43.020 --> 00:08:45.500
I tribute Big Waraji!

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:51.410
I Tribute Summon Superheavy Samurai 
Big Benkei in defense position!

00:08:53.900 --> 00:08:55.380
He brought it out!

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:59.490
Big Benkei is allowed to be summoned 
faceup in defense position!

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:04.480
Big Benkei can attack using 
its 3500 defense points!

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:06.850
Either Battleguard can be easily defeated!

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:08.290
I'm getting shivers!

00:09:08.700 --> 00:09:11.700
But it won't end in a single strike.

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:16.170
Ankokuji said that a friend 
is going to get pummeled.

00:09:16.170 --> 00:09:18.370
Was he talking about Yuya?

00:09:18.570 --> 00:09:21.800
When there are no spell or 
trap cards in my graveyard...

00:09:21.800 --> 00:09:24.710
...I can send one Superheavy Samurai 
in my hand to the graveyard

00:09:25.110 --> 00:09:29.080
to Special Summon this card from my hand!

00:09:30.180 --> 00:09:36.770
I Special Summon the Level 2 Tuner 
Monster Superheavy Samurai Trumpeter!

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:41.360
He brought out his Tuner Monster!

00:09:41.360 --> 00:09:43.940
He'll use it to tune Big Benkei!

00:09:43.940 --> 00:09:45.160
And Synchro Summon!

00:09:45.650 --> 00:09:46.670
Not good enough.

00:09:47.030 --> 00:09:50.300
I activate the trap Battleguard Sorcery!

00:09:52.120 --> 00:09:57.610
When there's a Battleguard on my field and 
you have at least two monsters on your field,

00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:00.760
I take control of one of your monsters!

00:10:00.760 --> 00:10:01.850
What?

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:06.040
I'll take Trumpeter!

00:10:11.220 --> 00:10:12.960
He stole his monster!

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:15.160
That means he can't Synchro Summon!

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:23.140
I did my research and knew that 
you were using Synchro to win!

00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:27.290
A match isn't solely decided on the field.

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:33.050
Even now, something is happening 
away from this field.

00:10:33.050 --> 00:10:36.820
If you don't hurry, I wonder what 
will happen to your dear friend.

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:39.350
Damn...  Yuya...

00:10:42.940 --> 00:10:44.720
I promise to get there.

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:47.240
Just wait, Gongenzaka!

00:10:50.030 --> 00:10:53.780
It's the first match in the second 
day of the Junior Youth Championship.

00:10:53.780 --> 00:10:59.240
Gongenzaka brought out the Tuner Monster 
Trumpeter in order to Synchro Summon,

00:10:59.240 --> 00:11:04.000
but Ankokuji took control of it.

00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:06.450
Your student is playing horribly.

00:11:06.450 --> 00:11:09.200
I can't believe he let his monster get taken.

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:12.650
That punk!  Are you trying 
to tarnish my reputation?

00:11:12.650 --> 00:11:14.670
I won't forgive you if you lose!

00:11:14.850 --> 00:11:16.660
If I don't hurry, Yuya will be...

00:11:16.870 --> 00:11:17.820
Let's battle!

00:11:18.220 --> 00:11:22.430
Big Benkei attacks Granite Battleguard!

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:28.970
Boulder Battleguard's effect activates!

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:33.700
Once per battle, it negates an 
attack against a Battleguard!

00:11:35.350 --> 00:11:36.710
He stopped it!

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:37.940
Damn!

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:40.450
I don't have much time!

00:11:40.680 --> 00:11:42.650
Why is he in such a hurry?

00:11:46.760 --> 00:11:50.320
Do you feel frustrated?  
Are you losing your cool?

00:11:50.320 --> 00:11:52.730
Not only did your precious 
monster betray you,

00:11:52.730 --> 00:11:56.080
but you don't know what's happening 
to your precious friend either.

00:11:56.080 --> 00:11:58.160
So it's natural to lose your cool.

00:11:59.100 --> 00:12:02.870
He definitely thinks you betrayed him.

00:12:03.020 --> 00:12:08.470
Because he believed that his friend would 
come rescue him, but you didn't show up!

00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:10.710
Damn!  Yuya!

00:12:11.100 --> 00:12:13.960
That's right.  Get more frustrated.

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:15.800
Lose your cool even more!

00:12:15.800 --> 00:12:20.190
The more you lose your cool, the more 
your heart and dueling fall apart.

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:26.140
I'll now prove how fragile 
your Immovable Duel is!

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:27.700
Gongenzaka!

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:31.160
Trust Yuya!

00:12:33.650 --> 00:12:36.700
Yuya told me not to worry!

00:12:36.920 --> 00:12:40.220
He promised to get your sash back!

00:12:40.220 --> 00:12:41.310
Yuya said that?

00:12:41.540 --> 00:12:44.380
Yuya is not like the Yuya of the past!

00:12:44.380 --> 00:12:46.450
He can battle on his own now!

00:12:46.900 --> 00:12:50.430
Noboru, now is the time to 
have an immovable heart!

00:12:50.750 --> 00:12:54.850
Believe in your friend and yourself!

00:12:56.400 --> 00:12:57.970
Father...

00:12:59.320 --> 00:13:01.540
So you were able to get in contact with him.

00:13:01.600 --> 00:13:04.800
How pathetic that the weakling 
is angry over nothing.

00:13:05.370 --> 00:13:09.800
He's no longer a weakling!

00:13:10.320 --> 00:13:13.360
I promise to get Gongenzaka's sash back!

00:13:13.360 --> 00:13:15.570
Yuya will definitely come here!

00:13:16.080 --> 00:13:17.220
What?

00:13:17.220 --> 00:13:18.810
Yuzu is right.

00:13:18.960 --> 00:13:22.050
Yuya is no longer the same as 
how he was three years ago!

00:13:22.300 --> 00:13:23.800
Gongenzaka...

00:13:26.050 --> 00:13:30.960
Now that I know Yuya's determination, 
my heart will no longer waver!

00:13:31.320 --> 00:13:34.400
I will simply do my own duel!

00:13:36.660 --> 00:13:40.000
That's right!  Keep going, Gongenzaka!

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:40.800
Get fired up!

00:13:40.800 --> 00:13:42.520
Get your blood boiling!

00:13:42.520 --> 00:13:44.340
Even if you tell him to keep going...

00:13:44.700 --> 00:13:46.590
I end my turn.

00:13:46.590 --> 00:13:48.090
What?  Really?

00:13:48.090 --> 00:13:50.310
Because he can't attack anymore.

00:13:51.040 --> 00:13:53.010
I believe in you, Yuya.

00:13:53.460 --> 00:13:56.400
You do your own duel!

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:04.660
Ladies and gentlemen!

00:14:04.880 --> 00:14:07.160
It's showtime!

00:14:10.300 --> 00:14:15.980
Witness Yusyo Sakaki-style 
entertainment dueling!

00:14:19.970 --> 00:14:20.840
Awesome!

00:14:20.840 --> 00:14:22.480
How fun!

00:14:28.380 --> 00:14:30.340
Trust?  Whatever!

00:14:30.850 --> 00:14:36.190
People will betray you, just like 
how your monster betrayed you!

00:14:36.530 --> 00:14:37.920
My turn!

00:14:41.280 --> 00:14:45.300
I tribute three monsters, 
including my Battleguards.

00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:58.010
I Special Summon Shaman 
Battleguard from my hand!

00:15:02.440 --> 00:15:03.440
What is that?

00:15:03.440 --> 00:15:05.680
It's so eerie that it gives me shivers!

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:08.770
Level 10 with only 2000 attack points?

00:15:08.770 --> 00:15:10.660
Something's up.

00:15:11.940 --> 00:15:13.480
Gongenzaka...

00:15:14.360 --> 00:15:15.710
Here I go!

00:15:15.710 --> 00:15:18.830
Shaman Battleguard's effect activates!

00:15:19.130 --> 00:15:23.070
Once per turn, I gain control 
of one of your monsters!

00:15:23.710 --> 00:15:28.540
I gain control of Big Benkei!

00:15:31.580 --> 00:15:33.060
This time, Big Benkei...

00:15:33.060 --> 00:15:34.960
...was taken!

00:15:35.180 --> 00:15:37.800
There's no one in the 
world that you can trust!

00:15:37.800 --> 00:15:40.700
You'll learn that by taking 
Big Benkei's attack!

00:15:40.700 --> 00:15:43.920
Let's battle!  Big Benkei 
attacks you directly!

00:15:47.680 --> 00:15:49.020
Watch out!

00:15:49.020 --> 00:15:52.360
If he takes Big Benkei's direct attack...

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:17.560
That was effective!  He instantly 
took 3500 points of damage!

00:16:17.560 --> 00:16:20.080
Are you okay, Gongenzaka?

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:21.290
Gongenzaka...

00:16:22.180 --> 00:16:23.580
I can't watch.

00:16:23.580 --> 00:16:25.800
He only has 500 life points left.

00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:28.530
Hey, stop making me look bad!

00:16:30.640 --> 00:16:33.220
You stopped at the edge of the cliff.

00:16:34.480 --> 00:16:37.150
With the next strike, it's game over!

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:40.380
It's pointless to stand up.

00:16:40.730 --> 00:16:46.620
You'll take Shaman Battleguard's 
attack and plummet into the ocean.

00:16:47.220 --> 00:16:50.720
No matter how much you believe in 
your friend, he isn't going to come.

00:16:50.720 --> 00:16:52.620
Yuya is coming!

00:16:53.110 --> 00:16:54.960
I believe in him!

00:16:55.330 --> 00:16:57.620
Then keep believing.

00:16:57.620 --> 00:17:02.840
Let's battle!  Shaman Battleguard, 
attack Gongenzaka directly!

00:17:03.340 --> 00:17:05.370
Finish him!

00:17:05.580 --> 00:17:11.110
At this moment, I banish Superheavy 
Samurai Gigagloves from my graveyard

00:17:11.500 --> 00:17:13.500
to draw a card from my deck.

00:17:13.500 --> 00:17:19.020
If that card is a Superheavy Samurai, 
your monster's attack points become 0!

00:17:25.370 --> 00:17:26.380
Come!

00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:30.930
Good!

00:17:33.570 --> 00:17:36.100
I believe in Yuya!

00:17:38.260 --> 00:17:41.310
Yuya will definitely come!

00:17:48.580 --> 00:17:53.050
No matter what happens, my unwavering 
heart will keep believing in my friends!

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:55.790
Well done!

00:17:55.790 --> 00:17:57.790
He's at the edge of a cliff,

00:17:57.790 --> 00:18:01.500
but he avoided his opponent's 
attack by the skin of his teeth!

00:18:02.480 --> 00:18:04.760
He was just lucky.

00:18:05.080 --> 00:18:07.640
But as long as I have Big Benkei,

00:18:07.640 --> 00:18:10.770
Shaman Battleguard can't be 
attacked due to its effect.

00:18:10.920 --> 00:18:15.380
Shaman Battleguard's effect only 
gains control of one monster.

00:18:15.380 --> 00:18:19.010
But if you bring out a monster 
stronger than Big Benkei next turn,

00:18:19.010 --> 00:18:21.250
I can exchange them!

00:18:21.520 --> 00:18:24.780
In other words, there's no way you can win.

00:18:25.440 --> 00:18:27.940
I end my turn.

00:18:29.180 --> 00:18:32.190
My father gave me this battle sash.

00:18:33.420 --> 00:18:37.150
But that's not what I need right now.

00:18:38.520 --> 00:18:41.100
What I need is...

00:18:41.100 --> 00:18:42.700
Gongenzaka!

00:18:47.220 --> 00:18:48.090
Yuya!

00:18:48.090 --> 00:18:49.440
Yuya!

00:18:49.940 --> 00:18:51.110
You came!

00:18:51.110 --> 00:18:52.800
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:55.820
Take this!

00:19:00.220 --> 00:19:04.790
Yuya, I received the sash from you!

00:19:05.110 --> 00:19:08.860
I believed in you, and you arrived!

00:19:09.140 --> 00:19:13.000
This is my battle sash now!

00:19:14.320 --> 00:19:16.000
My turn!

00:19:18.820 --> 00:19:25.620
I summon the Level 2 Tuner Monster 
Superheavy Samurai Battleball from my hand!

00:19:26.250 --> 00:19:31.280
A Tuner?  It's a weakling if 
you don't have another monster.

00:19:31.470 --> 00:19:38.190
Battleball can Synchro Summon using one 
Machine-Type monster on your field!

00:19:38.620 --> 00:19:39.770
What?

00:19:40.060 --> 00:19:48.260
Level 2 Battleball on my field tunes 
Level 8 Big Benkei on your field!

00:19:48.850 --> 00:19:53.540
Malevolent soul, along with the 
souls of a thousand blades,

00:19:53.540 --> 00:19:56.510
appear on the field in a whirling maelstrom!

00:19:57.310 --> 00:19:58.680
Synchro Summon!

00:19:59.380 --> 00:20:04.880
Arrive on the front lines, Level 10 
Superheavy Samurai Warlord Susanowo!

00:20:07.390 --> 00:20:09.760
He did it!  He Synchro Summoned!

00:20:09.760 --> 00:20:11.040
All right!

00:20:12.080 --> 00:20:18.300
Next, I equip Superheavy Samurai Soulbuster 
Gauntlet from my hand on to Susanowo!

00:20:24.080 --> 00:20:27.020
It gains 400 defense points!

00:20:29.650 --> 00:20:32.830
No way!  Just like Big Benkei, can it...

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:36.680
Yes!  It can attack using its defense points!

00:20:36.680 --> 00:20:37.420
Here I go!

00:20:37.970 --> 00:20:42.880
Battle, Susanowo!  Attack Shaman Battleguard!

00:20:43.540 --> 00:20:48.540
Due to Gigagloves's effect, Shaman 
Battleguard currently has 0 attack points!

00:20:48.540 --> 00:20:50.630
Since Susanowo has 4200 points...

00:20:50.630 --> 00:20:52.570
It will be over with a single strike.

00:20:52.570 --> 00:20:54.270
That gives me shivers!

00:20:57.170 --> 00:21:00.340
Kusanagi Sword Slash!

00:21:15.820 --> 00:21:22.820
The winner of the Junior Youth 
Championship's first match today is Gongenzaka!

00:21:24.760 --> 00:21:28.730
He finally won.  He made me nervous.

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:35.940
I believed that you would come, Yuya.

00:21:36.460 --> 00:21:39.900
I also believed that you 
would win, Gongenzaka.

00:21:42.380 --> 00:21:43.960
Yuya!

00:21:43.960 --> 00:21:46.640
We were worried.  Where were you?

00:21:46.640 --> 00:21:48.990
Sorry.  I'm up next.

00:21:48.990 --> 00:21:52.190
I'll do my best so that I'll 
be as great as Gongenzaka!

00:21:52.190 --> 00:21:55.120
Next is today's second match!

00:21:55.120 --> 00:22:02.800
Yuya Sakaki from You Show School vs 
Shingo Sawatari from Leo Duel School!

00:22:06.280 --> 00:22:07.850
Here I go!

00:22:13.030 --> 00:22:18.510
Catch the dream dancing in my heart
Release my falling tears

00:22:18.730 --> 00:22:27.990
I'll step out on to my first field
To meet my miracle  Fabulous One Step

00:22:34.880 --> 00:22:40.000
I realized that strength can't be given

00:22:40.260 --> 00:22:45.240
It's something I have to grab myself

00:22:45.530 --> 00:22:50.680
In that case, I have to keep moving
I can't stay still

00:22:50.930 --> 00:22:55.910
Even if walls and headwinds block my way

00:22:56.140 --> 00:23:01.540
I'll draw my trump card called 
"courage" to take a step forward

00:23:01.540 --> 00:23:05.960
I believe in my story of victory

00:23:06.250 --> 00:23:11.930
Everyone during battle is My Way
Duelists are being tested

00:23:11.930 --> 00:23:17.340
When times are tough, that's when you 
Smile, Jump, Fight & Step Up!

00:23:17.340 --> 00:23:22.640
Your smile is your Energy
Kick away your feelings of running away

00:23:22.640 --> 00:23:31.980
Jump into the new field
Shiny One Step that leads to the future

00:23:33.010 --> 00:23:40.230
One step... Just one step is fine
That's your Big Chance!!

00:23:45.710 --> 00:23:48.140
The cards are calling me.

00:23:48.140 --> 00:23:50.520
They're asking me to draw them.

00:23:50.520 --> 00:23:54.910
The lone star twinkling in the 
heavens!  Witness dueling's #1 star!

00:23:54.910 --> 00:23:56.920
The man who will defeat Yuya Sakaki!

00:23:56.920 --> 00:24:01.020
He's known as Neo New Sawatari!

00:24:01.020 --> 00:24:04.480
Neo New Sawatari is the best!

00:24:04.820 --> 00:24:09.940
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V:
Howling Whirlwind  Yosen Lost Tornado!

00:24:09.940 --> 00:24:12.840
The fun is only getting started!
